** 9.3 impurity sources       
* 18.03.2013 -> two types of impurity neutral sources
*              
* 1) Intrinsic: physical, chemical and self sputtering
*               here, self sputtering has also the meaing of reflection
*                (at present for given coefficients)
*                 fluid: RANDF <   chem  => sputtered
*               neutral: RANDF <= |chem| => sputtered
*              Impurity neutrals started with E0 with angle function of
*              F(theta)=sin(theta)**alpha*cos(theta)**beta 
*                alpha=1, beta=0: uniform distribution
*                alpha=1, beta=1: cosine  distribution
P_SPUT C_SPUT S_SPUT  ! physical, chemical, self sputtering
E_SPUT    SIN    COS  ! E0, Alpha, Beta
* 2) External points source
*              Alpha=1 default for this case, beta(>=0) must be given here
*              Further inputs:
*              E0 in eV:   energy
*              Strength in A: Flux
*              R,Z, Phi in cm and deg.: location
*              VR, VZ, VPHI: normalized, injection direction
*              IF VR=VZ=VPHI=0.: isotropic, same as beta=0